{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Image Authenticity.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Image Authenticity.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"image authenticity image authenticity","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Image Authenticity.md","fileName":"Image Authenticity.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Image Authenticity","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-16 00:47\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Image Authenticity and Forensic Reasoning]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Image Authenticity and Forensic Reasoning","fakephotos.epub"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Image Authenticity.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Image Authenticity.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"image authenticity image authenticity","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Image Authenticity.md","fileName":"Image Authenticity.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Image Authenticity","heading":"Image Authenticity","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"Image authenticity is the claim that a photograph represents an unaltered output of its stated capture process. Forensic examination cannot prove this claim absolutely: a clean result means only that the applied techniques did not find evidence of tampering under their operating conditions.\n\nNegative findings carry different weight for different files. A high-resolution image with intact metadata and strong physical cues is more testable than a compressed, downsampled, or stripped copy. Authentication is therefore an evidence-weighting judgment, not a binary property supplied by one tool.","tags":["baby"],"links":["Image Authenticity and Forensic Reasoning","fakephotos.epub"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Image Authenticity.md::2","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Image Authenticity.md","sourc